<speak>It came from them, which is encouraging. They pointed out that our old papers had grown around the way I worked. Someone would bring a bundle into my office, and I would know why each item was there because I had already been involved in the conversation. That does not work when decisions are distributed across the team. They now write down what the meeting is supposed to resolve. I still find myself supplying background that nobody has asked for, but at least I am beginning to notice when I do it.</speak>